# project: framework-2.0-release
VAR rc = 0

-> land_breaking_changes

=== land_breaking_changes ===
Land the 2.0 breaking changes on main, each covered by the migration guide.
Done when every breaking change has a documented migration path.
* [Breaking changes and migration guide landed] -> cut_rc

=== cut_rc ===
Cut the next release candidate and announce it to the community.
~ rc += 1
+ [RC published to the community] -> community_soak

=== community_soak ===
The RC soaks with the community for two weeks: collect regression reports
and test the top-50 ecosystem plugins against it.
+ [Regressions reported] -> fix_regressions
+ [More than a handful of top-50 plugins broke] -> add_compat_shims
+ [Two weeks clean] -> maintainer_vote

=== fix_regressions ===
Fix the reported regressions; fixes land in the next RC.
+ [Fixes ready for next RC] ~loop~ -> cut_rc

=== add_compat_shims ===
Add compatibility shims for the broken plugins before the next RC is cut.
+ [Shims in place] ~loop~ -> cut_rc

=== maintainer_vote ===
The maintainer group votes on the clean RC. Majority ships it; no majority
means one more RC cycle; past RC5 the vote becomes ship-or-abandon-2.0.
+ [Majority: ship 2.0] @human -> publish_2_0
+ {rc <= 5} [No majority: one more RC cycle] @human ~loop~ -> cut_rc
+ {rc > 5} [Past RC5, ship-or-abandon: ship it] @human -> publish_2_0
+ {rc > 5} [Past RC5, ship-or-abandon: abandon 2.0] @human -> abandon_2_0

=== publish_2_0 ===
Publish the 2.0 release and the migration blog post.
* [Published and announced] -> deprecation_window

=== deprecation_window ===
The 1.x branch stays supported for one quarter after 2.0 ships.
* [One quarter elapsed] -> deprecate_1x

=== deprecate_1x ===
Deprecate the 1.x branch.
* [1.x deprecated] -> END

=== abandon_2_0 ===
2.0 is abandoned; document the decision and wind down the RC line.
* [Wound down] -> END
